# Figma MCP Workflow

> Use the `figma-console` MCP server only (Desktop Bridge plugin). If unavailable, see `07-figma-console-mcp-connection.mdc` — do not silently fall back.

## When a Figma link is pasted

1. Verify the `figma-console` MCP connection (rule 07).
2. Parse `fileKey` and `nodeId` from the URL (convert `-` to `:` in `nodeId`).
3. Inspect the node via `figma-console` (component details, screenshot, variables).
4. Extract in order: name, variants/properties, nested components, auto-layout, styles (color, typography, spacing, corner radius, breakpoint).
5. Map every Figma style value to a token:
   - Color → CSS custom property in `src/styles/settings.scss` (`var(--color-*)`) — and its SCSS mirror (`$color-*`) for color functions
   - Font → CSS variable from the type scale in `src/styles/settings.scss` (`--font-size-*`, `--font-weight-*`, `--font-family-*`)
   - Spacing → nearest scale token from `src/styles/settings.scss`
   - Corner radius → nearest radius token
   - Breakpoint → nearest entry in `$breakpoints` (consumed via `b-up` / `b-d` / `b-btw` / `b-o` mixins in `src/styles/mixins.scss`)
6. Before building: summarize what you found and ask the user to confirm.

## Figma Layer Naming Conventions

Layers in Figma follow this naming convention (agreed with Bukovel design team):

- Component names: PascalCase with the `App` prefix — `AppButton`, `AppInput`, `AppCard`. Figma layer names may omit the prefix; the code identifier always includes it.
- Variants property: `Variant` — values: `primary`, `secondary`, `ghost`, `destructive`
- Size property: `Size` — values: `small`, `medium`, `large`
- State property: `State` — values: `default`, `hover`, `pressed`, `focus`, `disabled`, `loading`, `error`
- Boolean props: `Is` prefix — `IsDisabled`, `IsLoading`, `HasIcon`
- Theme variants when present: `Theme` — values: `summer`, `winter` (more themes may be added)

When Figma properties use different names, map them to the above convention in code and flag the discrepancy.

## Token Mapping Rules

### Colors

All color tokens live in `src/styles/settings.scss` as CSS custom properties on `:root[data-theme="..."]` selectors plus SCSS mirrors for use inside color functions.

Pattern:

```scss
:root[data-theme='summer'] {
  --color-primary: #1e6fff;
  --color-bg: #ffffff;
  --color-text: #0a0a0a;
  // ...
}

:root[data-theme='winter'] {
  --color-primary: #1e6fff; // currently same as summer
  // ...
}

// SCSS mirrors — only for places that need real Sass values (rgba, darken, etc).
$primary: #1e6fff;
$gray-100: #f5f5f5;
```

Multi-theme rules:

- All colors used in components MUST resolve via CSS variables so the component automatically restyles when `data-theme` changes
- New colors added during a build go into every existing theme (`summer`, `winter`, …), not just one
- Never reference SCSS mirrors directly inside component SCSS unless a color function requires it

Priority order for color token matching:

1. Exact match by role (e.g. button background → `var(--color-primary)`)
2. Nearest existing token
3. Flag as unmapped and ask

If no match exists:

- Confirm with the user
- Add the new CSS variable to every `data-theme` block in `src/styles/settings.scss`
- Add the SCSS mirror only if a color function will need it
- Never silently introduce a new hardcoded color in component SCSS

### Typography

Map Figma text styles to the type scale in `src/styles/settings.scss`. Typical token shape:

```
--font-family-base
--font-family-display
--font-size-xs    (12px)
--font-size-sm    (14px)
--font-size-md    (16px)
--font-size-lg    (18px)
--font-size-xl    (24px)
--font-size-2xl   (32px)
--font-size-3xl   (40px)
--font-weight-regular   (400)
--font-weight-medium    (500)
--font-weight-semibold  (600)
--font-weight-bold      (700)
--line-height-tight     (1.2)
--line-height-normal    (1.5)
```

If Figma uses a style not in the scale → flag it:
"Figma uses 15px / 600 which has no direct token match. Closest: `--font-size-md` + `--font-weight-semibold`. Use that, or add a new size to `settings.scss`?"

### Spacing

Round Figma spacing values to the nearest token from `src/styles/settings.scss`. Typical scale:

```
0px    → --size-0
4px    → --size-xs
8px    → --size-sm
12px   → --size-md
16px   → --size-lg
24px   → --size-xl
32px   → --size-2xl
48px   → --size-3xl
64px   → --size-4xl
```

If off-grid by more than 2px, flag it:
"Figma has `[X]px` here which is off the spacing scale. Rounding to `[nearest token]`. OK?"

### Corner Radius

Figma uses a `radius(N)` naming convention. `N` is a multiplier — the actual pixel value is `N × 4`. Token names live in `src/styles/settings.scss`:

```
radius(0)    = 0px   → --radius-none
radius(1)    = 4px   → --radius-xs
radius(2)    = 8px   → --radius-sm
radius(3)    = 12px  → --radius-md
radius(4)    = 16px  → --radius-lg
radius(5)    = 20px  → --radius-xl
radius(6)    = 24px  → --radius-2xl
radius(8)    = 32px  → --radius-3xl
radius(full) = 9999  → --radius-pill
```

If Figma shows a raw pixel number instead of `radius(N)`, flag it:
"`[LayerName]` has a raw `[X]px` corner radius instead of a named token. Nearest match: `var(--radius-Y)`. Should I use that, or should it be updated in Figma first?"

**Always check every object for missing corner radius.** If an object has no corner radius applied in Figma but visually looks like it should have one, flag it.

Never guess or invent a radius value. Always ask before proceeding.

### Breakpoints

Use the `$breakpoints` map in `src/styles/settings.scss` consumed via the mixins in `src/styles/mixins.scss`. Never write raw `@media (min-width: 768px)` in component SCSS.

```scss
@include b-up(md) {
  /* ≥ md breakpoint */
}

@include b-d(lg) {
  /* < lg breakpoint */
}
```

If Figma frame widths don't align with the existing breakpoints, flag it before adding a new one.

## Component Type Detection

Read the Figma layer hierarchy to determine component complexity, then place it accordingly:

- **Simple component**: single root element with no internal state shared across children (`AppButton`, `AppBadge`, `AppInput`, `AppText`, `AppCard`, `AppIcon`, …)
  → `src/components/App<Name>/` following `10-add-simple-component.mdc`.

- **Compound component**: a parent that owns state and shares it with named subcomponents (`AppModal`, `AppSheet`, `AppTabs`, `AppAccordion`, `AppDropdown`, `AppRadioGroup`, …)
  → `src/components/App<Name>/` with subcomponent files (`App<Name>.<Sub>.tsx`) and a context file (`App<Name>.context.ts`) following `11-add-compound-component.mdc`.

When uncertain which pattern applies, ask.

## After Every Build

1. Confirm with user: "Built `App<Name>` with states: `[list]`. Missing from Figma: `[list if any]`. Re-exported from `src/components/index.ts`. Showcase entry added at `/showcase/[slug]`."
2. If any tokens were unmapped or off-grid values rounded — summarize at the end.
3. If any objects had no corner radius applied in Figma — list them explicitly so the user can update Figma.
4. Auto-generate a `README.md` (see `05-quality-checks.mdc`).
